# nlohmann-json3-dev is deliberately absent: the tree vendors the header in
# third_party/nlohmann and CMake prefers find_package -> system headers ->
# vendored copy -> FetchContent, so the build never needs the -dev package.
# Listing it only made dpkg-checkbuilddeps fail on machines that had the
# vendored path satisfied.
#
# GoogleTest is likewise not listed: tests/ pulls it via FetchContent, and the
# Debian build sets BL_BUILD_TESTS=OFF anyway.
Standards-Version: 4.7.0
Rules-Requires-Root: no
Homepage: https://github.com/wiczajac666/bucharestlite

Package: bucharest-lite
Architecture: any
Depends: ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends}
Description: Bucharest Lite - open-source non-linear video editor (NLE)
 A GPL-3.0 licensed NLE built on Qt6/C++17 with FFmpeg for media IO.
 Features include multi-track timeline, codec plugins (h264, vp9, av1, theora,
 mpeg4, aac, flac, vorbis, opus), CPU compositing preview, audio mixing,
 timeline editing (trim, split, ripple, 3-point editing), and export pipeline.
 .
 Bucharest Lite is a non-linear video editor (NLE) that supports multi-track
 editing, keyframeable clip properties, transitions, effects, color grading,
 chroma key compositing, subtitle support, and audio mixing. Projects are
 saved as JSON files and can include relative media paths. Export supports
 MP4, MKV, and WebM containers with H.264, VP9, AV1, and AAC codecs.
 .
 WWW: https://github.com/wiczajac666/bucharestlite